  "title": "A compositional inverse for the support polynomials of comb preorder polytopes",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Let tau_0 be empty, and for every integer n>=0 obtain tau_(n+1) by taking the disjoint union of tau_n with a singleton and then adjoining a new minimum. Let Q_n consist of the nonnegative real vectors on the 2n vertices satisfying sum_(v in I) x_v <= |I| for every lower ideal I of tau_n, and let h_n(t)=sum_(a in Q_n intersect Z^(2n)) t^(number of positive coordinates of a), with h_0(t)=1. For an indeterminate t, define F(t,x)=sum_(n>=0) t^(-n) h_n(t) x^(n+1) and R(t,x)=sum_(m>=1) (-1)^(m-1) [1+(1+t)^m t^(1-m) sum_(j=0)^(m-2) t^j] x^m, where the inner sum is zero for m=1. Then R(t,F(t,x))=x=F(t,R(t,x)) in Q(t)[[x]]. Equivalently, the same R is x/[(1+x)(1+(1+t)x)(1+(1+t)x/t)] and is the compositional inverse of the full support-refined comb generating series. This is the entire identity frozen in source.md, with no restriction to a finite range or scalar specialization of t.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
